(2192724, 297690, 21714, '<td valign="top">Excellent! I did find it to be a bit over-sharpened, but still I find it really beautiful. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but just going through the entries, this is one of the images that stopped me.</td>', 'Excellent! I did find it to be a bit over-sharpened, but still I find it really beautiful. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but just going through the entries, this is one of the images that stopped me.', '2006-03-01 09:52:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192770, 297442, 8367, '<td valign="top">You did a great job on this. I''ve been trying to get the same look with my dog. I can''t believe you pulled off 15 seconds! My dog''s gone after two. ;) I think the shadows on the wall hurt your score and some voters just don''t like pet photos and won''t take the time to even look at the photo...it''s their loss. The duotone conversion/tones are great. If I was nit-picking, the photo could be slightly rotated ccw.</td>', 'You did a great job on this. I''ve been trying to get the same look with my dog. I can''t believe you pulled off 15 seconds! My dog''s gone after two. ;) I think the shadows on the wall hurt your score and some voters just don''t like pet photos and won''t take the time to even look at the photo...it''s their loss. The duotone conversion/tones are great. If I was nit-picking, the photo could be slightly rotated ccw.', '2006-03-01 10:14:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192774, 298468, 14509, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i> Hard to believe that the person capable of taking this thoughtful and beautiful photograph could also come up with such an awful title.  But title aside, it''s one of the most interesting images in the challenge.  Very fine work.  7. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I appreciate your opinion. My original title was "Soaring High". Perhaps I should have used that instead. Is there a way I can change it. I am new to DPC?<br/>Diana</td>', 'Originally posted by ubique: Hard to believe that the person capable of taking this thoughtful and beautiful photograph could also come up with such an awful title.  But title aside, it''s one of the most interesting images in the challenge.  Very fine work.  7.   I appreciate your opinion. My original title was "Soaring High". Perhaps I should have used that instead. Is there a way I can change it. I am new to DPC?Diana', '2006-03-01 10:15:52.000000', NULL, 0),
