(2192790, 298375, 37200, '<td valign="top">This is a really nice duotone.  I love the luminousity of the lights being tinted, and the shadows even being blue, and not too much drops to black.  The patterns and textures are nice.  Just a nice shot all around!</td>', 'This is a really nice duotone.  I love the luminousity of the lights being tinted, and the shadows even being blue, and not too much drops to black.  The patterns and textures are nice.  Just a nice shot all around!', '2006-03-01 10:22:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192792, 297547, 22872, '<td valign="top">ditto on what bosterlobster said!  I''ve been looking into the different fisheyes and this is the one that I keep coming back to.<br/> <br/>Great photo!<br/> <br/></td>', 'ditto on what bosterlobster said!  I''ve been looking into the different fisheyes and this is the one that I keep coming back to. Great photo! ', '2006-03-01 10:22:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192793, 298548, 27484, '<td valign="top">Wow. Thanks to everybody who took the time to make constructive comments and push me up into third place.  I had a feeling all along that I was fighting for third place along with the Tiger picture and of course the other Moving Rock picture - the top two were in a league of their own.<br/> <br/>Living on the East Coast, I find it hard to compete with the scenic photos from Iceland or the Western US. So I knew I had my shot to get something good when I visited Death Valley and was luckily able to come away with some great pics.<br/> <br/>I was pretty surprised to see another Moving Rock picture and even more amazed that people made comments simply to tell me there was another one like mine.  I actually took a bunch looking the other way like gaurawa did, but I prefered the rock in the foreground.<br/> <br/>For those that asked how the rocks move... nobody knows.  Just type in "Racetrack Moving Rocks" into Google and you''ll get a bunch of theories.  It''s an interesting place.</td>', 'Wow. Thanks to everybody who took the time to make constructive comments and push me up into third place.  I had a feeling all along that I was fighting for third place along with the Tiger picture and of course the other Moving Rock picture - the top two were in a league of their own. Living on the East Coast, I find it hard to compete with the scenic photos from Iceland or the Western US. So I knew I had my shot to get something good when I visited Death Valley and was luckily able to come away with some great pics. I was pretty surprised to see another Moving Rock picture and even more amazed that people made comments simply to tell me there was another one like mine.  I actually took a bunch looking the other way like gaurawa did, but I prefered the rock in the foreground. For those that asked how the rocks move... nobody knows.  Just type in "Racetrack Moving Rocks" into Google and you''ll get a bunch of theories.  It''s an interesting place.', '2006-03-01 10:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192798, 297481, 52292, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by thegrandwazoo:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice play on words. No instead of Now. Could be sharper and the image needs to be bigger 640 by X. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks for your comment. So, you now these words? I wrote "no" because i don''t want to change ;) I know that it''s normally "now" =)</td>', 'Originally posted by thegrandwazoo: Nice play on words. No instead of Now. Could be sharper and the image needs to be bigger 640 by X.   thanks for your comment. So, you now these words? I wrote "no" because i don''t want to change ;) I know that it''s normally "now" =)', '2006-03-01 10:24:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2192805, 297978, 37200, '<td valign="top">Awsome depth!  This *really* came to life with editing when compared to the original.  Beautiful!</td>', 'Awsome depth!  This *really* came to life with editing when compared to the original.  Beautiful!', '2006-03-01 10:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
