(2193741, 297955, 37893, '<td valign="top">I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;) <br/> <br/>My first impression of this image is that it a very nicely rendered duotone which is spot on with the challenge requirements. In as much as I am not quite fond with photos with a green tint to them, this works somehow.<br/> <br/>I think what hurts this image is the missed vertical of the pole behind the boat and the blown highlights at the upper left hand corner. In addition to that, the "dirty" snow doesn''t add much to the over all feel of this photo. I would try to do this as a sepia and I bet the results would be quite different.<br/> <br/>Keep on practicing but most improtantly have fun! This is a great image! <br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;)  My first impression of this image is that it a very nicely rendered duotone which is spot on with the challenge requirements. In as much as I am not quite fond with photos with a green tint to them, this works somehow. I think what hurts this image is the missed vertical of the pole behind the boat and the blown highlights at the upper left hand corner. In addition to that, the "dirty" snow doesn''t add much to the over all feel of this photo. I would try to do this as a sepia and I bet the results would be quite different. Keep on practicing but most improtantly have fun! This is a great image!  Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 15:30:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193744, 296859, 15711, '<td valign="top">This should have rated so much higher. I love it.</td>', 'This should have rated so much higher. I love it.', '2006-03-01 15:30:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193753, 297408, 37893, '<td valign="top">I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;) <br/> <br/>My first impression of this image is that it definitely has the age old feel of medieval castles that you see in old photos. The reflections are a great touch and definitely gets the most bang for your money with this shot. What hurts this image IMHO is the fact that you broke one of the major rules of photography. You situated your horizon line smack in the middle of the composition. There are time when this "breaking the rule" technique works but it doesn''t for this image. I believe the crop is too tight on top. If the building was situated more on the right to give ample space on the left for trees I think this would look well balanced.<br/> <br/>Keep on practicing but most improtantly have fun! This is a great image! <br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;)  My first impression of this image is that it definitely has the age old feel of medieval castles that you see in old photos. The reflections are a great touch and definitely gets the most bang for your money with this shot. What hurts this image IMHO is the fact that you broke one of the major rules of photography. You situated your horizon line smack in the middle of the composition. There are time when this "breaking the rule" technique works but it doesn''t for this image. I believe the crop is too tight on top. If the building was situated more on the right to give ample space on the left for trees I think this would look well balanced. Keep on practicing but most improtantly have fun! This is a great image!  Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 15:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193762, 298455, 41746, '<td valign="top">I thought this cutie would end much higher. Great photo, Lesley. But you can´t win all the time :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-01 15:49:34.</i></td>', 'I thought this cutie would end much higher. Great photo, Lesley. But you can´t win all the time :)', '2006-03-01 15:38:51.000000', '2006-03-01 15:49:34.000000', 0),
(2193767, 297801, 51974, '<td valign="top">Dustin, <br/> <br/>You should check out the website of a photographer named Chris Jordan. His "Laid to Waste" series has a photgraph of this same shop front. A friend o mine is actually considering buying the photo (not cheap, either) and when he showed it to me, I remembered seeing yours in this challenge. Weird coincidence. I kind of prefer your shot to his.<br/> <br/>Here''s his URL:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.chrisjordan.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">chrisjordanphotography</a> <br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Tony Tuck<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-01 15:41:33.</i></td>', 'Dustin,  You should check out the website of a photographer named Chris Jordan. His "Laid to Waste" series has a photgraph of this same shop front. A friend o mine is actually considering buying the photo (not cheap, either) and when he showed it to me, I remembered seeing yours in this challenge. Weird coincidence. I kind of prefer your shot to his. Here''s his URL: chrisjordanphotography  Cheers,  Tony Tuck', '2006-03-01 15:40:26.000000', '2006-03-01 15:41:33.000000', 0),
(2193774, 297411, 37893, '<td valign="top">I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful.<br/> <br/>My first impression of this image is that it is has a certain old feel flavor to it. In as much as the duotone color selection works for this entry, the image in itself does not hold my attention for too long. It might just be the POV you used or it could be that there are just way to many thing happening here. In as much as the textures add layer and depth to the image, it is also a bit distracting. The DOF could have been adjusted to isolate one from the other so that the other accents the major subject of focus. I think digital grain would also help this one if your intent was to go for the old image feel.<br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful. My first impression of this image is that it is has a certain old feel flavor to it. In as much as the duotone color selection works for this entry, the image in itself does not hold my attention for too long. It might just be the POV you used or it could be that there are just way to many thing happening here. In as much as the textures add layer and depth to the image, it is also a bit distracting. The DOF could have been adjusted to isolate one from the other so that the other accents the major subject of focus. I think digital grain would also help this one if your intent was to go for the old image feel. Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 15:43:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193799, 298730, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hiya Pidge :) Huggies to my couch mate ;)<br/> <br/>I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;) <br/> <br/>So let''s get on with the show ;) You seem to have a fond affinity with ice these days ;) The image in itself is quite plain eventhough textures and layers abound throughout the composition. I have seen your other ice images and by far they stand out more than this image. The purple duotone used on this image doesn''t lead me to think of cold harsh winters. Maybe a blueish tint would have been more effective. A close up view would have been more effective as well. The bokeh is nice but I think the bokeh would scream and sing out loud had this been a closer study of one of the leaves ;)<br/> <br/>I hope this helps Pidge ;)<br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'Hiya Pidge :) Huggies to my couch mate ;) I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful in your pursuit to improve your photos ;)  So let''s get on with the show ;) You seem to have a fond affinity with ice these days ;) The image in itself is quite plain eventhough textures and layers abound throughout the composition. I have seen your other ice images and by far they stand out more than this image. The purple duotone used on this image doesn''t lead me to think of cold harsh winters. Maybe a blueish tint would have been more effective. A close up view would have been more effective as well. The bokeh is nice but I think the bokeh would scream and sing out loud had this been a closer study of one of the leaves ;) I hope this helps Pidge ;) Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 15:50:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193827, 297801, 45318, '<td valign="top">Interesting. I didn''t know of this photographer or his project. Some cool pics there..I have a few pics of Katrina Damaged areas I need to PS. Ill post some soon..thanks for the heads up!</td>', 'Interesting. I didn''t know of this photographer or his project. Some cool pics there..I have a few pics of Katrina Damaged areas I need to PS. Ill post some soon..thanks for the heads up!', '2006-03-01 15:59:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193833, 296487, 37893, '<td valign="top">I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful :)<br/> <br/>First off, the focus is a bit soft. It almost looks as if you ran this through NI several times specially since you were shooting at such a high ISO. The left side has far too much blown highlights for voters to overlook. The image is so smooth overall that there isn''t much contrast and texture to hold a viewer in place.<br/> <br/>I love these types of shots. I have a few of then actually. What makes photo-journalistic type shots effective is good DOF and textures ;)<br/> <br/>I hope I could help in any way.<br/> <br/>Cheers, <br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'I hope you see my comment as constructive and helpful :) First off, the focus is a bit soft. It almost looks as if you ran this through NI several times specially since you were shooting at such a high ISO. The left side has far too much blown highlights for voters to overlook. The image is so smooth overall that there isn''t much contrast and texture to hold a viewer in place. I love these types of shots. I have a few of then actually. What makes photo-journalistic type shots effective is good DOF and textures ;) I hope I could help in any way. Cheers,  Rikki', '2006-03-01 16:00:33.000000', NULL, 0),
