(2193878, 298640, 40718, '<td valign="top">A few things.  It''s probably better to rotate the canvas so the shower tiles are parallel with the border (unless you go for an obvious tilt for effect).  The technicals are not bad.  The lighting is nice without too much glare and the focus is sharp.  I''m not quite sure that this was the best shot for duotone as the tone doesn''t seem to add too much to the picture.  In the end, we may not have enough to keep our interest.  The 103 5 scores show that people didn''t have a big beef with the shot, but also didn''t get wowed by it.</td>', 'A few things.  It''s probably better to rotate the canvas so the shower tiles are parallel with the border (unless you go for an obvious tilt for effect).  The technicals are not bad.  The lighting is nice without too much glare and the focus is sharp.  I''m not quite sure that this was the best shot for duotone as the tone doesn''t seem to add too much to the picture.  In the end, we may not have enough to keep our interest.  The 103 5 scores show that people didn''t have a big beef with the shot, but also didn''t get wowed by it.', '2006-03-01 16:22:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193905, 298162, 41531, '<td valign="top">wow, what an amazing picture, love the simplicity as well as the DOF, congrats and yr placing, you have outdone yourself!</td>', 'wow, what an amazing picture, love the simplicity as well as the DOF, congrats and yr placing, you have outdone yourself!', '2006-03-01 16:32:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193927, 296628, 53091, '<td valign="top">beautiful!!</td>', 'beautiful!!', '2006-03-01 16:38:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2193995, 296628, 53668, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, ex. Kiwi!</td>', 'Congratulations, ex. Kiwi!', '2006-03-01 16:57:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194032, 298204, 48524, '<td valign="top">The perspective and DOF is really working for me, as well as the composition.  The guitar strings really draws the eye into the picture.  However, I want to say the lighting on the hand is just a bit too harsh, the focus on the nails a little soft.  The worn fingernails are a very nice detail, and I would have liked to see them better in focus.  Also, I''m not a great fan of the color tint you chose (personally would have preferred less purple and more sepia) but that''s your call.<br/> <br/>Very nice shot overall.</td>', 'The perspective and DOF is really working for me, as well as the composition.  The guitar strings really draws the eye into the picture.  However, I want to say the lighting on the hand is just a bit too harsh, the focus on the nails a little soft.  The worn fingernails are a very nice detail, and I would have liked to see them better in focus.  Also, I''m not a great fan of the color tint you chose (personally would have preferred less purple and more sepia) but that''s your call. Very nice shot overall.', '2006-03-01 17:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194066, 296179, 48524, '<td valign="top">First thing that strikes me is the biker...in my opinion I really don''t think it''s helping the shot any.  Part of it might be the position of the motorcycle and part of it might be that I feel like it would be better off without him all together...the bridge just has that nice peaceful feel to it and it''s like the motorcycle disturbs it.  Composition-wise, I think that the bridge could have been emphasize more if taken from a different angle, either being able to see more inside of it or from further out to the side...the way it is now it''s like the side of the bridge that we can see just blends into the sky, and there isn''t much detail on the inside, either.  I do like the way the tree branches seem to frame it, and the color tint you chose complements it very well.<br/> <br/>I''d have say I like your first outtake better; it incorporates the biker into the shot more and while you can''t see the outer shape of the bridge as much, I like the tunnel feeling it has.</td>', 'First thing that strikes me is the biker...in my opinion I really don''t think it''s helping the shot any.  Part of it might be the position of the motorcycle and part of it might be that I feel like it would be better off without him all together...the bridge just has that nice peaceful feel to it and it''s like the motorcycle disturbs it.  Composition-wise, I think that the bridge could have been emphasize more if taken from a different angle, either being able to see more inside of it or from further out to the side...the way it is now it''s like the side of the bridge that we can see just blends into the sky, and there isn''t much detail on the inside, either.  I do like the way the tree branches seem to frame it, and the color tint you chose complements it very well. I''d have say I like your first outtake better; it incorporates the biker into the shot more and while you can''t see the outer shape of the bridge as much, I like the tunnel feeling it has.', '2006-03-01 17:15:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194072, 296628, 32602, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the blue! Sensational shot!!!!</td>', 'Congratulations on the blue! Sensational shot!!!!', '2006-03-01 17:16:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194081, 296458, 48524, '<td valign="top">Ouch, I have the same dead pixel problem with my camera (though mine generates about 10 of them--be thankful you only have one XP).  Since it''s basic editting I think dead pixels are easily forgiven, though.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I really like this shot, the lighting is very well done.  I love the viginette feel, and the top of the screw head really stands out.  It''s got a very abstract feel to it, but it doesn''t seem sloppy or chaotic, either.  A couple of the hotspots are a little distracting, but not too much to affect it overall.  I only wish it were a little easier to make out the figure of the sax player.</td>', 'Ouch, I have the same dead pixel problem with my camera (though mine generates about 10 of them--be thankful you only have one XP).  Since it''s basic editting I think dead pixels are easily forgiven, though. Anyway, I really like this shot, the lighting is very well done.  I love the viginette feel, and the top of the screw head really stands out.  It''s got a very abstract feel to it, but it doesn''t seem sloppy or chaotic, either.  A couple of the hotspots are a little distracting, but not too much to affect it overall.  I only wish it were a little easier to make out the figure of the sax player.', '2006-03-01 17:19:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194133, 298281, 47487, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5. I thought it was an OK image. Reasons I didn''t vote it higher:<br/> <br/>I thought it was just that little bit TOO yellow, just for my taste.<br/>The lights are overexposed.<br/>The composition feels a little out of balance. You have the lamp post pretty much on a thirds line, but then you have the (street? runway?) going straight down the middle. It just feels a little awkward to look at; there''s nowhere to let the eyes come to rest somehow.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I gave this a 5. I thought it was an OK image. Reasons I didn''t vote it higher: I thought it was just that little bit TOO yellow, just for my taste.The lights are overexposed.The composition feels a little out of balance. You have the lamp post pretty much on a thirds line, but then you have the (street? runway?) going straight down the middle. It just feels a little awkward to look at; there''s nowhere to let the eyes come to rest somehow. ', '2006-03-01 17:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194144, 297970, 47487, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this one. I''d have probably given it a 5 -- a decently shot photo of something that doesn''t really SPEAK to me (remember we couldn''t see your comments) but which is visually interesting. I think a slightly greater depth of field might have helped you a bit; if there''s some significance to the bit of beadless string (the focal point) I don''t know it.<br/></td>', 'I didn''t vote on this one. I''d have probably given it a 5 -- a decently shot photo of something that doesn''t really SPEAK to me (remember we couldn''t see your comments) but which is visually interesting. I think a slightly greater depth of field might have helped you a bit; if there''s some significance to the bit of beadless string (the focal point) I don''t know it.', '2006-03-01 17:40:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194150, 297055, 47487, '<td valign="top">I think it might have been more of a WOW image if the road led into the frame, or down the middle, rather than out of it. Even so I''d have given this a 7 or so if I''d made it that far in the voting; the tones are very nice and I like your choice of subject.</td>', 'I think it might have been more of a WOW image if the road led into the frame, or down the middle, rather than out of it. Even so I''d have given this a 7 or so if I''d made it that far in the voting; the tones are very nice and I like your choice of subject.', '2006-03-01 17:43:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2194158, 298685, 47487, '<td valign="top">Gave it a six because I like lines and it was technically fine. :) Other than that, I didn''t really get the point of it; I imagine a lot of people felt the same.<br/> <br/>Shooting out of the box is fantastic. Just don''t expect the results to do well at this particular site unless you''re an absolute PS whiz, popular enough to have a "following", or extremely lucky...</td>', 'Gave it a six because I like lines and it was technically fine. :) Other than that, I didn''t really get the point of it; I imagine a lot of people felt the same. Shooting out of the box is fantastic. Just don''t expect the results to do well at this particular site unless you''re an absolute PS whiz, popular enough to have a "following", or extremely lucky...', '2006-03-01 17:48:06.000000', NULL, 0),
