(2209172, 298851, 37673, '<td valign="top">From the CC<br/> <br/>Very well done. The detail is amazing. Your focus on this shot is exceptional and I doubt could have been better. The DOF is interesting it works quite well with the shot. It isolates the subject very well and doesn''t take waway any attention from the subject. Lighting is great. The shadows show excellent depth as well as definition. The only distraction is the little hair in the lower right but it''s not too bad. You really hit the challenge hear as far as subject It really is a precious moment. Very well done and congrats on a great shot.</td>', 'From the CC Very well done. The detail is amazing. Your focus on this shot is exceptional and I doubt could have been better. The DOF is interesting it works quite well with the shot. It isolates the subject very well and doesn''t take waway any attention from the subject. Lighting is great. The shadows show excellent depth as well as definition. The only distraction is the little hair in the lower right but it''s not too bad. You really hit the challenge hear as far as subject It really is a precious moment. Very well done and congrats on a great shot.', '2006-03-07 23:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209199, 296487, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>I wanna start off by saying that this is my favorite type of shot to critique and I''m glad I pulled it from the queue.  What do I mean by this?  It may not be the most excellent shot, but there is so much potential there that I have to stop and look again!<br/> <br/>This critique begs for my what I like and what I don''t like format...<br/> <br/>What I like!  You captured an incredible moment in time.  The look on the gentlemans face is priceless!  He has an incredible pride in what he does and it shows in his expression and your capture.  He also has incredible character.  I love the taped together glasses and his wonderful grin.  There are layers of great texture and leading lines in this shot.  The texture is in the eggs and egg crating.  The lines are there both in the eggs and the space that they are displayed.  You obviously used a wide angle lens.  This is apparent in the overall feel of the shot.  Not having seen the original, I would say that your choice to go b/w is a good one but I can''t be 100 percent on that point.<br/> <br/>What I don''t like.  This is a bit harder.  Everything in the crop left of the post on the left third line is unneeded.  It distracts and detracts from the shot.  A lot of that portion of the shot is blown out which doesn''t help anything...  You shot is a touch skewed.  It''s not level.  A little more skewed and it would look artsy.  The way it is now looks like you didn''t take time to straighten the shot in camera.  Looks a little sloppy.  You are a touch soft here.  Most times I like soft focus, but this looks more like it is OOF or your focal point is in the wrong place.  I may be wrong on this issue but without seeing a full sized original I can''t tell.  You lose your subjects left (right in image) elbow in the shadows of the background.  The subjects dark clothing against the dark background is a bit of a distraction.<br/> <br/>I truly like this shot.  I like the overall compostion minus the left side of the frame.  I love the character of the subject.  I love the textures.  If I was you, I would see if he would let me shoot him again.  It may take a couple of tries, but I see an potential award winning shot here.  Please, keep shooting!  If you go back and shoot this subject again, PLEASE post your results here!  I will be watching for it.<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: I wanna start off by saying that this is my favorite type of shot to critique and I''m glad I pulled it from the queue.  What do I mean by this?  It may not be the most excellent shot, but there is so much potential there that I have to stop and look again! This critique begs for my what I like and what I don''t like format... What I like!  You captured an incredible moment in time.  The look on the gentlemans face is priceless!  He has an incredible pride in what he does and it shows in his expression and your capture.  He also has incredible character.  I love the taped together glasses and his wonderful grin.  There are layers of great texture and leading lines in this shot.  The texture is in the eggs and egg crating.  The lines are there both in the eggs and the space that they are displayed.  You obviously used a wide angle lens.  This is apparent in the overall feel of the shot.  Not having seen the original, I would say that your choice to go b/w is a good one but I can''t be 100 percent on that point. What I don''t like.  This is a bit harder.  Everything in the crop left of the post on the left third line is unneeded.  It distracts and detracts from the shot.  A lot of that portion of the shot is blown out which doesn''t help anything...  You shot is a touch skewed.  It''s not level.  A little more skewed and it would look artsy.  The way it is now looks like you didn''t take time to straighten the shot in camera.  Looks a little sloppy.  You are a touch soft here.  Most times I like soft focus, but this looks more like it is OOF or your focal point is in the wrong place.  I may be wrong on this issue but without seeing a full sized original I can''t tell.  You lose your subjects left (right in image) elbow in the shadows of the background.  The subjects dark clothing against the dark background is a bit of a distraction. I truly like this shot.  I like the overall compostion minus the left side of the frame.  I love the character of the subject.  I love the textures.  If I was you, I would see if he would let me shoot him again.  It may take a couple of tries, but I see an potential award winning shot here.  Please, keep shooting!  If you go back and shoot this subject again, PLEASE post your results here!  I will be watching for it. YoursTC', '2006-03-07 23:30:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209202, 297967, 37673, '<td valign="top">From the CC<br/> <br/>Very clever title. This is nicely done. The lighting is very soft and well placed. Composition is great I like the balance you have created in the shot. Not at all revealing yet a strong and sensual. The skin tones are smooth and well done. My only complaint is the lack of contrast but, that is my personal opinion. Overall I think you did very well. Please tell your wife she has NOTHING to be self consious about.</td>', 'From the CC Very clever title. This is nicely done. The lighting is very soft and well placed. Composition is great I like the balance you have created in the shot. Not at all revealing yet a strong and sensual. The skin tones are smooth and well done. My only complaint is the lack of contrast but, that is my personal opinion. Overall I think you did very well. Please tell your wife she has NOTHING to be self consious about.', '2006-03-07 23:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209227, 298530, 37673, '<td valign="top">From the CC<br/> <br/>How come I always wind up with the photos that have NOTHING to critique. All I can say is MAGNIFICANT. This shot is so well done. Everything about this picture is IMO perfect. I''m actually at a loss for words here. Very well done.</td>', 'From the CC How come I always wind up with the photos that have NOTHING to critique. All I can say is MAGNIFICANT. This shot is so well done. Everything about this picture is IMO perfect. I''m actually at a loss for words here. Very well done.', '2006-03-07 23:35:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209229, 298720, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Blue Bella" is nice entry into the Duotone challenge.  I remember this shot because I have personally wanted to go to the Bellagio for so long.  I really like your choice of blue, it seems very appropriate for the subject. The other color options would probably have the image with a very different and not as appealing feel.  <br/> <br/>The photograph itself is overall appealing.  Very nice time of day to take the shot.  The lighting on the building is accenting the structure very nicely.  The light at the top of the tower looks a little bit over blown.  Also the sky looks very processed, I am not sure if it is the time lapse or just the editing.  Its not too distracting at first glance, but when you spend some time with the image it starts to pop out.  Overall the image is still nice and I could see it making a nice postcard.  Keep up the good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Blue Bella" is nice entry into the Duotone challenge.  I remember this shot because I have personally wanted to go to the Bellagio for so long.  I really like your choice of blue, it seems very appropriate for the subject. The other color options would probably have the image with a very different and not as appealing feel.   The photograph itself is overall appealing.  Very nice time of day to take the shot.  The lighting on the building is accenting the structure very nicely.  The light at the top of the tower looks a little bit over blown.  Also the sky looks very processed, I am not sure if it is the time lapse or just the editing.  Its not too distracting at first glance, but when you spend some time with the image it starts to pop out.  Overall the image is still nice and I could see it making a nice postcard.  Keep up the good work.', '2006-03-07 23:35:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209266, 297881, 37673, '<td valign="top">From the CC<br/> <br/>Very nice shot. I love the choice of color. The composition was put together nicely and shows some thought. The texture and shadows work so well together here. It shows incredible depth. You did well here and IMO I can''t find anything wrong with it other than it''s not hanging in my living room. Well done.</td>', 'From the CC Very nice shot. I love the choice of color. The composition was put together nicely and shows some thought. The texture and shadows work so well together here. It shows incredible depth. You did well here and IMO I can''t find anything wrong with it other than it''s not hanging in my living room. Well done.', '2006-03-07 23:42:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209284, 297302, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Strolling in the park" is a very nice addition into the Duotones challenge.  Interesting choice to go with the gray scale, I would be curious to see it in sepia it give is a warmer feel.  <br/> <br/>The overall image is nice.  The subject itself is different from the run of the mill park.   With the curving path and the two people showing how massive the trees and the world around us is, gives a wonderful subject.  I wish the contrast had been turned up so there was more definition between the trees, the leaves and the path.   I love the overall image.  I personally would have gone with a black border because the gray almost brings out the flatness from lack of contrast or try it without a border at all.  Looking at your profile, I really wonder if you wanted the image to be soft like it is.  But of course photography is a form of art which in the end is seen different by the artists and the audience.  I really love the heath, keep up the good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Strolling in the park" is a very nice addition into the Duotones challenge.  Interesting choice to go with the gray scale, I would be curious to see it in sepia it give is a warmer feel.   The overall image is nice.  The subject itself is different from the run of the mill park.   With the curving path and the two people showing how massive the trees and the world around us is, gives a wonderful subject.  I wish the contrast had been turned up so there was more definition between the trees, the leaves and the path.   I love the overall image.  I personally would have gone with a black border because the gray almost brings out the flatness from lack of contrast or try it without a border at all.  Looking at your profile, I really wonder if you wanted the image to be soft like it is.  But of course photography is a form of art which in the end is seen different by the artists and the audience.  I really love the heath, keep up the good work.', '2006-03-07 23:48:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209368, 297777, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Gris" is a lovely portrait done in Duotones and meets the challenge.   I think the challenge become extremely hard when we have 600+ entries, especially because I think voters do get burned out or they only vote on the 20% they like.  Taking all that is consideration I am really glad to see you were in the top 30%.<br/> <br/>The image is is very nice and clean.  I think the most appealing attribute is the eyes, I am sure it is just my preceptive but that is what captured my attention.  The light being captured by her eyes is almost enchanting.  The lighting you used is wonderful.  The light across the face accents just prefectly without createing any harsh sahdows.  Also I think your lighting displays itself in the highlights it is able to pick up out of her hair.  The focus is very nice.  I really don''t see anything I would change or even want to try.  I personally would be extremely proud of this image. <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Gris" is a lovely portrait done in Duotones and meets the challenge.   I think the challenge become extremely hard when we have 600+ entries, especially because I think voters do get burned out or they only vote on the 20% they like.  Taking all that is consideration I am really glad to see you were in the top 30%. The image is is very nice and clean.  I think the most appealing attribute is the eyes, I am sure it is just my preceptive but that is what captured my attention.  The light being captured by her eyes is almost enchanting.  The lighting you used is wonderful.  The light across the face accents just prefectly without createing any harsh sahdows.  Also I think your lighting displays itself in the highlights it is able to pick up out of her hair.  The focus is very nice.  I really don''t see anything I would change or even want to try.  I personally would be extremely proud of this image. ', '2006-03-08 00:13:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2209758, 298749, 50056, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe you didn''t score in top 10 on this, I love it.  The model is perfect and it is so well "executed"...one of my faves!!  I''d buy a print of this one...people must not "get it" or something.</td>', 'I can''t believe you didn''t score in top 10 on this, I love it.  The model is perfect and it is so well "executed"...one of my faves!!  I''d buy a print of this one...people must not "get it" or something.', '2006-03-08 01:50:38.000000', NULL, 0),
